/**
 * The literal union of every published article id.
 *
 * This lives in the corpus package, not in services/router.ts, because it is
 * corpus data: create-article appends to it on every publish. Keeping it in the
 * router made the article generator write into the site on every run, which is
 * one of the things that pinned the generator to the site repository
 * (issue #4974 item 3).
 *
 * Direction matters for the package boundary: the site may import from the
 * package, never the reverse. This file has no imports at all, so it stays
 * within the confinement rule (tests/packages-articles-confinement.test.ts)
 * and can be consumed by both sides.
 *
 * Split into chunks because a single union this long is slow to check and
 * produces unreadable diffs; the split is mechanical and carries no meaning.
 */

